  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a rectangular grid with NNN rows and MMM columns. A number Ai,jA_{i,j}Ai,j​ is written in the cell belonging to the ithi^{th}ith row and the jthj^{th}jth column.\n\n\nAi,j=1A_{i,j} = 1Ai,j​=1, for all 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N and 1≤j≤M1 \\leq j \\leq M1≤j≤M, except for i=Ni = Ni=N and j=Mj = Mj=M.\nAN,M=0A_{N, M} = 0AN,M​=0.\nFind the number of sub-rectangular grids which contain only 111s.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of testcases. Then the testcases follow.\nEach testcase contains of a single line of input, two integers N,MN, MN,M.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, print the number of sub-rectangular grids containing only 111s.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤501 \\leq T \\leq 501≤T≤50",
      "2≤N,M≤1042 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^42≤N,M≤104",
      "Subtasks",
      "30 points : 2≤N,M≤202 \\leq N, M \\leq 202≤N,M≤20",
      "70 points : 2≤N,M≤1042 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^42≤N,M≤104"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2 2\n4 5",
        "output": "5\n130",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case-1: Consider the following rectangles :\n\nRectangle made up of cell (1,1)(1,1)(1,1).\nRectangle made up of cell (1,2)(1,2)(1,2).\nRectangle made up of cell (2,1)(2,1)(2,1).\nRectangle made up of cells (1,1)(1,1)(1,1) and (1,2)(1,2)(1,2).\nRectangle made up of cells (1,1)(1,1)(1,1) and (2,1)(2,1)(2,1).\n\nTotal 555 sub-rectangles of given grid are made up of only 111s."
      }
    ]
  },
